{
  "project": "discount-used-cars",
  "title": "Discount Used Cars and Trucks: site demo, part A",
  "notes": [
    "Times in each capture are seconds from that capture's frame 0. A scene plays capture seconds [scene.trimSec, scene.trimSec + scene.durationSec].",
    "Selectors were read from clients/discount-used-cars-site/src (Home.tsx, Layout.tsx) and checked on the running preview at 1440x900 and 390x797.",
    "clock pins the page's wall clock to a Wednesday 2 PM in Houston, so the site shows 'Open Now' (it is computed from the time).",
    "The phone capture is 390x797: under iOS's 47 pt status bar that makes the iPhone 14 screen, 390x844 pt, exactly (capturing 844 tall would stretch the phone or put the header under the Dynamic Island).",
    "Site content outside the on-screen fact list is hidden at capture time with the shot's injected css (the site source is untouched): shots 3 and 4 blur the Discover tiles' '$205/mo' and '4.8/5' figures and the '24 Google reviews' label (a Screen Studio style privacy blur; 'Hola. / Se habla español' and 'Easy financing' stay sharp); shot 2 hides the lineup fine print ('15% down, 12.9% APR, 48 months') with visibility:hidden, so the layout and every scroll target are unchanged. Delete the css lines and recapture to show them.",
    "Part B (the sale desk) is inserted between shots 4 and 5: shot 4 ends held at 1.8x on the 'Admin · Staff Sign-In To The Sale Desk' row with the cursor resting on it, so part B can open on the click (same window, same 1440x900 viewport at DSF 2).",
    "Shot 5 stops on the Trucks card: one more swipe reaches the lineup's fine print (finance terms), which is not in the on-screen fact list.",
    "Shots 3 and 4 anchor their last/first scroll on the Discover tiles, not the review: the review carousel changes the quote's height every 6 s, which moved a quote-anchored scroll by ~100 px between the two captures.",
    "Shot 2 parks the real mouse in the left page gutter (x 64) while the cursor is hidden during the first scroll: otherwise the cursor carried over from shot 1 (342, 579) sits over the cards as they scroll past, and the Trucks card is already in its hover state (photo zoomed, white arrow) before the visible cursor reaches it.",
    "Shot 3's set-up click on the finder waits for the section's 0.9 s reveal transition (translateY 28 px): clicking mid-reveal put the cursor 4.7 px below where shot 2 ended. The typing ends 0.73 s before frame 0, so the caret is in the same blink phase as shot 2's last frame."
  ],
  "base": "http://localhost:5183",
  "serve": {
    "build": "cd clients/discount-used-cars-site && VITE_DESK_URL=https://desk.discountusedcarsandtrucks.com npx vite build --outDir $SCRATCH/dist-demo --emptyOutDir",
    "preview": "cd clients/discount-used-cars-site && npx vite preview --outDir $SCRATCH/dist-demo --port 5183 --strictPort"
  },
  "capture": {
    "command": "node .claude/skills/recordly-demo/scripts/capture.cjs --storyboard .claude/skills/recordly-demo/examples/discount-used-cars/storyboard.json --shot <id> --out $SCRATCH/captures/<id> --publish clients/discount-used-cars-demo/public/shots --clean",
    "order": [
      "1-hero",
      "2-scroll",
      "3-buy",
      "4-menu",
      "5-phone"
    ],
    "dsf": 2,
    "dsfReason": "The window shows the 1440 px page ~1490 px wide and zooms up to 1.8x (≈2680 px): DSF 1 is visibly soft there, DSF 2 stays sharp (self-test dsf-compare-at-1.8x.png)."
  },
  "fps": 30,
  "size": [
    1920,
    1080
  ],
  "introKey": "discount.intro.seen",
  "clock": "2026-09-30T14:00:00-05:00",
